e.","gap":null,"note":"`allInterpolatedIsomorphic (r s : ℝ≥0∞) (hr : 1 < r) (hs : 1 < s) : Nonempty (NormalTracialEquiv (interpolatedTrace r) (interpolatedTrace s) (interpolatedTopology r) (interpolatedTopology s))`: every pair of interpolated free group factors L(F_r), L(F_s) with r,s ∈ (1,∞] (integer ranks via `groupVonNeumann (FreeGroup (Fin n))`, `FreeGroup ℕ` for ∞, and non-integer r as the corner of `L(F_2) ⊗ B(ℓ²)` by a projection of trace `1/√(r-1)`) is related by a *-isomorphism that preserves the canonical trace and is ultraweakly bicontinuous. The summary's statement L(F_2) ≅ L(F_3) and all interpolated factors; the fundamental-group conclusion is a consequence, not stated.","reading":"reading:1edf0b8f984d37c72f6e9123","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:5937ba79c80864ee10f2fb0a","reading:1edf0b8f984d37c72f6e9123"],"state":"different-scope-descriptions"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"755c4b729512c7e2c7d1d3303eb9706f5adf1681","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners (.github/workflows/openai-math-kernel.yml), one j","name":"Carlos Toledo, cert-machine","pin":"9814e4c06281e34a113ce853d7d99ccce160b750","repository":"https://github.com/carlostoledo1891/cert-machine","source":"cert-machine","url":"https://carlostoledo.co/reports/openai-math.html"},"id":"reading:5937ba79c80864ee10f2fb0a","pair_review":false,"review_state":"outside-report","source":"cert-machine","source_term":"NARROWER — DECLARED","source_value":{"code":"NARROWER — DECLARED","confide